  id: S01_20
  era: "2nd millennium BCE \xB7 Section 1 \xB7 Prehistoric India \xB7 c. 1.5 million years ago \u2013 700 BCE"
  title: Copper tools
  text: "Copper was smelted and hammered into axes, chisels, fish-hooks and bangles. Because copper was scarce and soft, stone blades stayed in use. The Copper Hoards of the Ganga\u2013Yamuna doab include harpoons and human-shaped figures."
